.TH "METADUMP" "1" "October 23, 2026" "ka9q-radio" "ka9q-radio Manual"
.SH NAME
metadump \- decode and display ka9q-radio control/status packets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B metadump
.RI "[options] [-r radio | radio]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
metadump prints decoded TLV command/status packets. With a selected SSRC it
sends status polls; without one it listens passively. Normal output includes
receive time, sender socket, packet kind, and decoded fields. Input is the
control/status multicast group name/address.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-r radio, \-\-radio radio"
Select the control/status destination, alternatively supplied as a positional
argument.
.TP
.B "\-s ssrc, \-\-ssrc ssrc"
Poll and filter for a channel SSRC. The default is to listen passively.
The special value 0 refers to the front end parameters shared by all channels.
.TP
.B "\-a, \-\-all"
Request all-channel status using the reserved broadcast SSRC. See current
limitations below.
.TP
.B "\-c count, \-\-count count"
Exit after this many accepted packets. Default two. Command packets can count
as well as status packets.
.TP
.B "\-i seconds, \-\-interval seconds"
Set polling interval, default one second.
.TP
.B "\-n, \-\-newline"
Print decoded fields on separate lines.
.TP
.B "\-t, \-\-stdin"
Read and decode one binary packet from standard input, then exit. Input must
begin with the command/status byte; do not include IP/UDP headers.
.TP
.B "\-o source, \-\-source source"
Restrict network reception to one source.
.TP
.B "\-R count, \-\-retries count"
Set resolver retry count, default zero.
.TP
.B "\-l locale, \-\-locale locale"
Set locale, overriding $LANG environment if set.
.TP
.B "\-v, \-\-verbose"
Increase diagnostics.
.TP
.B "\-V, \-\-version"
Print version and exit.
.SH LIMITATIONS
A passive run can wait indefinitely if no
matching packets arrive.
.SH EXAMPLES
Poll a known channel and display each TLV separately:
.PP
.nf
metadump \-n \-s 10000000 \-c 2 hf.local
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
radiod(8), tune(1), powers(1)
.PP
Project documentation: https://github.com/ka9q/ka9q-radio
